64
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:11,000
About recruiting scouts, there was basically two ways that this happens.

65
00:05:11,340 --> 00:05:19,460
The first way is a boy is a Weeblos, and he transitions into a Boy Scout troop.

66
00:05:19,460 --> 00:05:26,340
In my experience, about eight out of ten boys were Weeblos and transitioned from a Weeblos

67
00:05:26,340 --> 00:05:27,859
den into our troop.

68
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:30,919
The second group of people is everybody else.

69
00:05:31,419 --> 00:05:35,180
So there are Weeblos, and there is everybody else.

70
00:05:35,679 --> 00:05:41,039
Now, I'm not going to go into a long, in-depth talk about transitioning Weeblos into your Scout

71
00:05:41,039 --> 00:05:41,299
troop.

72
00:05:41,460 --> 00:05:43,580
I'll give you a very quick three-step plan.

73
00:05:43,580 --> 00:05:46,099
First, find all the Weeblos dens.

74
00:05:46,740 --> 00:05:50,780
Try and maintain contact with them and offer them camping opportunities.

75
00:05:51,080 --> 00:05:52,280
Offer them a den chief.

76
00:05:52,780 --> 00:05:57,320
Offer them anything that they would need in the way of resources that a Scout troop would

77
00:05:57,320 --> 00:05:57,659
have.

78
00:05:57,900 --> 00:06:01,620
Stay in touch with them throughout the year, and we don't ever give up.

79
00:06:02,440 --> 00:06:07,460
So that is my little three-step plan for recruiting Weeblos.

80
00:06:07,460 --> 00:06:14,299
Very oversimplified, but recruiting everybody else is a totally different ball of wax.

81
00:06:14,460 --> 00:06:15,400
Totally different story.

82
00:06:16,200 --> 00:06:21,099
Now, through the force of gravity, we get a couple of Newtonian Scouts every year.

83
00:06:21,320 --> 00:06:26,219
And what I mean by that is we have a Scout troop, and we have a decent program.

84
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:32,539
Somebody hears about that and decides that they want to come visit, and bada bing, they

85
00:06:32,539 --> 00:06:33,679
end up being a Boy Scout.

86
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:37,360
That happens pretty rarely, to tell you the truth.

87
00:06:37,820 --> 00:06:44,260
The next way we're going to approach everybody else are the kind of cold call methods, like

88
00:06:44,260 --> 00:06:47,780
school visits and open houses and things like that.

89
00:06:47,860 --> 00:06:50,720
Just recruiting Scouts from the general population.

90
00:06:51,500 --> 00:06:57,060
Frankly, I can't recall recruiting more than one or two Scouts this way in many, many years.

91
00:06:57,500 --> 00:07:01,240
Tremendously little return for the amount of effort that goes into it.

92
00:07:01,240 --> 00:07:05,900
And I don't know as I can recommend them to you, this kind of cold calling.

93
00:07:06,340 --> 00:07:08,380
I can recommend some more promising ways.

94
00:07:08,700 --> 00:07:12,360
Here is a little quick and dirty math.

95
00:07:12,520 --> 00:07:18,440
My best guess, about 10,000 boys need to see a TV commercial for one of them to be interested

96
00:07:18,440 --> 00:07:22,060
enough to hunt down a Scout troop and actually become a Scout.

97
00:07:22,060 --> 00:07:30,780
For every 500 boys who hear a direct mass appeal, like school visits or something like that,

98
00:07:31,060 --> 00:07:32,460
I think you get one guy.

99
00:07:33,260 --> 00:07:34,540
That's my experience.

100
00:07:34,920 --> 00:07:43,140
For every 10 or 15 boys who are approached by a friend who is already a Scout, you get

101
00:07:43,140 --> 00:07:44,400
one Scout.

102
00:07:44,400 --> 00:07:48,239
So you see the ratios are starting to get a little more promising.

103
00:07:49,780 --> 00:07:52,760
10,000 to 1 for broadcast type appeal.

104
00:07:53,179 --> 00:07:58,780
500 to 1 for a direct mass appeal, like a school presentation or something like that.

105
00:07:59,179 --> 00:08:04,219
10 or 15 to 1 for a one-on-one appeal from a peer.

106
00:08:04,220 --> 00:08:11,240
And then I would say you might even have a slightly better ratio, maybe 5 or 10 to 1, if a boy's

107
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:17,000
parents are approached by other parents who they know and trust, whose son is a part of

108
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:17,320
Scouting.

109
00:08:17,700 --> 00:08:19,660
Where do we want to concentrate our efforts?

110
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:24,900
To my mind, we want to concentrate on the two most promising approaches.

111
00:08:25,420 --> 00:08:32,300
That 10 to 15 for one for every boy who is approached by a peer who is in Scouting.

112
00:08:32,299 --> 00:08:37,380
And that 5 or 10 to 1 for a parent-to-parent type contact.

113
00:08:37,719 --> 00:08:42,919
One way that we're going to celebrate the centennial this year is to do a little bit of recruiting

114
00:08:42,919 --> 00:08:47,920
on a very personal basis, one-to-one, peer-to-peer, boy-to-boy.

115
00:08:48,859 --> 00:08:55,699
I am very proud to tell you that we came to the attention of our Chief Scout Executive, Bob

116
00:08:55,699 --> 00:08:56,560
Mazzucca.

117
00:08:56,560 --> 00:09:02,760
He has mentioned us specifically a couple of times, and I was able to get a recording

118
00:09:02,760 --> 00:09:03,119
of it.

119
00:09:03,979 --> 00:09:05,400
Scout units are even getting...

120
00:09:05,400 --> 00:09:07,500
I don't know where Kenneth Square, Pennsylvania is.

121
00:09:07,640 --> 00:09:09,260
Anybody know where Kenneth Square, Pennsylvania is?

122
00:09:09,979 --> 00:09:10,420
Near Philly.

123
00:09:11,780 --> 00:09:12,400
Troop 24.

124
00:09:13,880 --> 00:09:15,540
Take notes, Steve, because this is cool.

125
00:09:15,819 --> 00:09:17,459
Troop 24, Kenneth Square, Pennsylvania.

126
00:09:17,699 --> 00:09:19,479
These kids have gotten together and they've made a pledge.

127
00:09:19,480 --> 00:09:23,260
They've pledged they're going to earn 100 merit badges and rank advancements.

128
00:09:24,080 --> 00:09:28,840
They're going to do 100 extra hours of community service over and above what they normally do.

129
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:35,820
And they're going to invite 100 boys who aren't in Scouting to get in Scouting.

130
00:09:36,020 --> 00:09:36,780
Now think about that.

131
00:09:36,840 --> 00:09:39,760
Think what would happen if every pack and troop and crew in the country did that.

132
00:09:40,300 --> 00:09:45,980
Think what would happen if every person in this room told just 10 people, not 100 people,

133
00:09:45,980 --> 00:09:47,540
about the magic of Scouting.

134
00:09:47,680 --> 00:09:53,260
What would happen as we rekindled that fire and got people fired up so you're all deputized

135
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:57,040
into the army of evangelists go out there and talk about Scouting.

136
00:09:58,060 --> 00:10:03,700
So that's our chief executive talking about this recruiting plan.

137
00:10:03,820 --> 00:10:10,120
What my realistic expectation is, is that it would be absolutely astoundingly wonderful

138
00:10:10,120 --> 00:10:15,320
if we got 10 Scouts out of that effort.

139
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:18,860
I would be very curious to know about other recruiting efforts.

140
00:10:19,280 --> 00:10:25,180
A lot of them are very localized and are very effective on a local basis.

141
00:10:25,760 --> 00:10:31,260
I'd be interested to know what you do and how you manage recruiting where you are.

142
00:10:31,260 --> 00:10:34,960
These are the days that we're camping out here.

143
00:10:35,140 --> 00:10:37,420
We're camping inside the outdoors.

144
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:40,800
Who knows the way to our camp?

145
00:10:40,920 --> 00:10:44,420
It's out here and we're camping out on the shore.

146
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:48,820
Cause these are the days that we're camping out here.

147
00:10:49,060 --> 00:10:51,440
We're camping inside the outdoors.

148
00:10:52,320 --> 00:10:54,720
Do you know the way to our camp?

149
00:10:54,800 --> 00:10:58,340
It's out here and we're camping out on the shore.

150
00:10:59,260 --> 00:11:02,320
We don't want to work no more.

151
00:11:02,320 --> 00:11:08,160
I'm marked by a lack of truth.

152
00:11:09,360 --> 00:11:13,940
The world turns to Mason, Scoutmaster.

153
00:11:13,940 --> 00:11:29,140
As a Scoutmaster, I am familiar with the privations required to lead my Scouts to ever-increasing heights of achievement.

154
00:11:29,140 --> 00:11:41,500
I will precede them in this perambulation as an example of what can be earned through honest exertion.

155
00:11:41,500 --> 00:11:44,120
Yeah, well Mr. Mason, that's really some mountain there.

156
