00:13:19,820 --> 00:13:23,080
Richard Mason Scoutmaster.

181
00:13:23,080 --> 00:13:24,600
I thank you for joining us.

182
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:36,140
We'll be right back.

183
00:13:38,340 --> 00:13:43,540
We'll be right back.

184
00:13:43,540 --> 00:14:08,380
Write me a letter

185
00:14:08,380 --> 00:14:10,599
Send it by mail

186
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:13,740
Email that is, folks.

187
00:14:14,320 --> 00:14:17,340
And here's an answer to one of your emails.

188
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:28,840
So here's an email I received from somebody

189
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:33,800
who is asking me some questions about the way that their son's troop is run.

190
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:38,080
I'm not going to get into all the little details about this

191
00:14:38,080 --> 00:14:41,600
because the overarching thing that we want to talk about

192
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:45,540
is the way parents and boys experience scouting.

193
00:14:45,720 --> 00:14:46,720
There's a little bit of a difference

194
00:14:46,720 --> 00:14:48,860
between the way a parent experiences scouting

195
00:14:48,860 --> 00:14:50,300
and a boy experiences scouting.

196
00:14:50,740 --> 00:14:53,920
And what are your options when you discover

197
00:14:53,920 --> 00:14:57,000
that the troop that your son has joined

198
00:14:57,000 --> 00:15:00,740
is not really running on all eight cylinders,

199
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:02,420
that they don't actually get it

200
00:15:02,420 --> 00:15:05,120
and they're kind of bending the scout program around.

201
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:08,800
The way that this came to me was

202
00:15:08,800 --> 00:15:12,819
this mom was talking with her son

203
00:15:12,819 --> 00:15:15,599
about the way that cooking merit badge was going.

204
00:15:17,140 --> 00:15:23,060
And it was her opinion that the scout master

205
00:15:23,060 --> 00:15:24,939
was adding requirements to the badge.

206
00:15:25,660 --> 00:15:27,240
And from what she explained to me,

207
00:15:27,240 --> 00:15:28,620
I would have to agree.

208
00:15:29,460 --> 00:15:33,200
And so her question really boiled down to this.

209
00:15:34,520 --> 00:15:35,880
Do I leave this alone

210
00:15:35,880 --> 00:15:38,480
or can I bring this up in a positive manner

211
00:15:38,480 --> 00:15:39,560
so it can be dealt with?

212
00:15:39,700 --> 00:15:41,180
I mean, these are trained leaders,

213
00:15:41,480 --> 00:15:43,540
but I don't see the boys being trained

214
00:15:43,540 --> 00:15:44,560
in how to run the troop.

215
00:15:45,040 --> 00:15:46,620
There really isn't much scout advancement

216
00:15:46,620 --> 00:15:48,620
or activities taking place or the meetings.

217
00:15:49,280 --> 00:15:51,460
And if there are, it's pretty rare.

218
00:15:51,460 --> 00:15:56,540
And female opinions seem to be seen as meddling.

219
00:15:57,520 --> 00:15:59,340
They lost about six boys this year

220
00:15:59,340 --> 00:16:02,120
due to what I believe was just a lack of interest.

221
00:16:02,840 --> 00:16:03,680
So what's your take?

222
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:07,260
Well, I replied this way.

223
00:16:07,760 --> 00:16:12,440
You basically have three options in this situation.

224
00:16:13,340 --> 00:16:16,080
The situation that she describes isn't all that unusual.

225
00:16:16,900 --> 00:16:19,240
You know, we want parents to be involved

226
00:16:19,240 --> 00:16:21,440
and we want them to look in and see what's going on.

227
00:16:21,500 --> 00:16:22,440
And if they have questions,

228
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:24,160
we want to be able to answer their questions.

229
00:16:25,020 --> 00:16:27,480
And, you know, she didn't get a very satisfactory answer

230
00:16:27,480 --> 00:16:28,560
from this scout master.

231
00:16:28,900 --> 00:16:31,920
And unfortunately, in the way that things go,

232
00:16:32,400 --> 00:16:35,040
a lot of us guys tend to kind of blow off

233
00:16:35,040 --> 00:16:37,700
the questions that we get from moms

234
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:39,300
because we see them as being meddling.

235
00:16:41,400 --> 00:16:45,900
So that's just a bad attitude to begin with.

236
00:16:46,380 --> 00:16:48,360
And here are the three choices that I outlined.

237
00:16:48,360 --> 00:16:50,740
One is that you can fix the troop.

238
00:16:51,520 --> 00:16:54,360
Two is that you can live with things the way that they are.

239
00:16:54,740 --> 00:16:56,840
And three is that you can find another troop.

240
00:16:57,080 --> 00:16:58,640
So let's talk about fixing the troop.

241
00:16:59,300 --> 00:17:00,880
You know that it rarely works.

242
00:17:01,440 --> 00:17:03,480
If six scouts have left the troop

243
00:17:03,480 --> 00:17:06,000
and the adult leaders can't figure out why,

244
00:17:07,020 --> 00:17:09,860
then they're unlikely to listen to a mom.

245
00:17:10,280 --> 00:17:12,000
They're unlikely to listen to anyone.

246
00:17:12,620 --> 00:17:14,079
They're unlikely to listen to me.

247
00:17:14,339 --> 00:17:15,980
They're unlikely to listen to a commissioner

248
00:17:15,980 --> 00:17:17,839
or a group of parents or anything.

249
00:17:17,839 --> 00:17:21,500
The only real power brokers in a scout troop

250
00:17:21,500 --> 00:17:23,300
are the head of the chartering organization

251
00:17:23,300 --> 00:17:25,379
and the chartered organization representative.

252
00:17:26,379 --> 00:17:28,060
And for them to make changes,

253
00:17:28,179 --> 00:17:29,939
they have to understand there's a problem.

254
00:17:30,320 --> 00:17:32,300
And then they have to take appropriate action,

255
00:17:32,840 --> 00:17:36,540
which unfortunately usually leads to a big upset

256
00:17:36,540 --> 00:17:38,760
and several of the adult leaders leaving

257
00:17:38,760 --> 00:17:40,139
and a lot of hard feelings.

258
00:17:40,140 --> 00:17:42,280
And it can really be a killer.

259
00:17:44,280 --> 00:17:46,820
My advice, don't try number one.

260
00:17:46,980 --> 00:17:48,160
Don't try to fix the troop.

261
00:17:48,360 --> 00:17:49,180
It's not going to work.

262
00:17:49,700 --> 00:17:50,740
It almost never does.

263
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:53,280
If it does, it's a giant upset.

264
00:17:54,300 --> 00:17:59,620
Now, if there were some kind of youth protection issues going on,

265
00:17:59,680 --> 00:18:02,640
if there were these flagrantly inappropriate things happening,

266
00:18:03,100 --> 00:18:04,140
that's another question.

267
00:18:04,140 --> 00:18:07,400
But this is kind of a fine question of, you know,

268
00:18:07,700 --> 00:18:09,240
one advancement requirement.

269
00:18:10,460 --> 00:18:12,840
Number two, leaving things as they are.

270
00:18:13,940 --> 00:18:16,780
What you really have to do if you're a parent

271
00:18:16,780 --> 00:18:18,300
is you need to honestly determine

272
00:18:18,300 --> 00:18:20,280
who's having a problem with the situation.

273
00:18:21,140 --> 00:18:23,400
Now, if the son is happy

274
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:26,000
and enjoys scouting with his friends

275
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:27,080
and his present troop,

276
00:18:27,580 --> 00:18:29,280
you might just want to leave things alone.

277
00:18:29,280 --> 00:18:31,200
Given that there are a lot of scout troops,

278
00:18:31,340 --> 00:18:32,940
just as described here,

279
00:18:33,360 --> 00:18:35,980
you know, who really sometimes don't get it,

280
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:39,500
there are many scouts who are perfectly satisfied

281
00:18:39,500 --> 00:18:40,960
with their experience in scouting.

282
00:18:42,399 --> 00:18:45,260
Number three is to find another troop.

283
00:18:45,980 --> 00:18:48,440
If the son, not the parent,

284
00:18:48,620 --> 00:18:50,960
but if the son is truly dissatisfied

285
00:18:50,960 --> 00:18:52,240
and unhappy with his troop,

286
00:18:52,860 --> 00:18:54,320
if he's given it his best shot,

287
00:18:54,560 --> 00:18:56,240
if he's found the experience wanting,

288
00:18:56,720 --> 00:18:58,960
it's probably time to start shopping around

289
00:18:58,960 --> 00:18:59,760
and look for another troop.

290
00:18:59,880 --> 00:19:01,880
You know, scouts are free to join any troop they want.

291
00:19:02,460 --> 00:19:04,120
And don't let anybody tell you any different.

292
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:07,580
I would go visit a few local troops with your son

293
00:19:07,580 --> 00:19:09,800
and see how he reacts to them

294
00:19:09,800 --> 00:19:11,320
and then ask plenty of questions

295
00:19:11,320 --> 00:19:12,900
of the adult leaders

296
00:19:12,900 --> 00:19:14,600
and assure yourself that they get it.

297
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:17,780
Now, here are some key indicators that they get it,

298
00:19:18,140 --> 00:19:19,420
at least in my mind.

299
00:19:20,640 --> 00:19:23,840
Youth leaders would be elected by scouts,

300
00:19:24,060 --> 00:19:25,260
not appointed by leaders.

301
00:19:26,220 --> 00:19:28,160
The patrol leaders council would meet

302
00:19:28,160 --> 00:19:29,380
at least once a month.

303
00:19:30,100 --> 00:19:31,700
The youth leaders are running the meeting,

304
00:19:32,700 --> 00:19:34,000
really actually running the meeting,

305
00:19:34,100 --> 00:19:36,400
not just doing what the scoutmaster tells them to do.

306
00:19:37,060 --> 00:19:39,540
The scoutmaster himself has plenty of time

307
00:19:39,540 --> 00:19:40,880
to talk to you

308
00:19:40,880 --> 00:19:43,720
because they don't really have anything to do

309
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:44,680
during a troop meeting.

310
00:19:45,540 --> 00:19:46,760
Camping trips and activities

311
00:19:46,760 --> 00:19:48,940
are planned by the patrol leaders council.

312
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:51,720
Scouts are advancing at their own speed.

313
00:19:51,980 --> 00:19:53,440
I mean, there's no advancement schedule

314
00:19:53,440 --> 00:19:55,300
or merit badges being taught at troop meetings

315
00:19:55,300 --> 00:19:56,340
or anything like that.

316
00:19:57,159 --> 00:19:59,220
A troop that's operated as outlined

317
00:19:59,220 --> 00:20:02,440
is going to have happy, engaged scouts

318
00:20:02,440 --> 00:20:03,399
who advance regularly,

319
00:20:03,560 --> 00:20:05,340
not because they're compelled to by a plan,

320
00:20:05,720 --> 00:20:07,020
but because they're out scouting.

321
00:20:08,680 --> 00:20:11,340
Troops like this may look a little chaotic at first,

322
00:20:11,460 --> 00:20:12,560
but under the surface,

323
00:20:12,780 --> 00:20:13,919
they have a lot of heart.

324
00:20:13,920 --> 00:20:16,460
So if you take my advice,

325
00:20:17,100 --> 00:20:21,380
you're going to either leave things as they are

326
00:20:21,380 --> 00:20:23,680
or you're going to find another troop.

327
00:20:24,380 --> 00:20:27,300
Now, at the age of, you know,

328
00:20:27,380 --> 00:20:30,240
between 10 and a half and 11 or 12,

329
00:20:30,760 --> 00:20:31,600
that's a young guy.

330
00:20:32,160 --> 00:20:34,940
And he's in the troop for his first couple of years

331
00:20:34,940 --> 00:20:36,600
and the most important things to him

332
00:20:36,600 --> 00:20:38,740
are first and foremost his friends.

333
00:20:39,640 --> 00:20:41,640
And that's a pretty important part of scouting

334
00:20:41,640 --> 00:20:43,700
because if he's in there with his buddies

335
00:20:43,700 --> 00:20:45,200
and he's having a decent time,

336
00:20:45,960 --> 00:20:46,760
there you go.

337
00:20:47,280 --> 00:20:50,640
That, to me, answers most of the question right there.

338
00:20:51,580 --> 00:20:54,160
He may be concerned with advancements

339
00:20:54,160 --> 00:20:55,880
and he may really like to go camping

340
00:20:55,880 --> 00:20:57,600
and, you know,

341
00:20:57,760 --> 00:21:00,840
those are both important aspects of the program.

342
00:21:01,360 --> 00:21:02,860
And he's also going to be concerned

343
00:21:02,860 --> 00:21:04,760
about how he's treated by the adult leaders.

344
00:21:05,580 --> 00:21:06,600
But, you know,

345
00:21:06,660 --> 00:21:08,720
those are the three main things that are in his mind

346
00:21:08,720 --> 00:21:12,680
and that affect how he is experiencing the scout program.

347
00:21:13,700 --> 00:21:14,940
You'll know pretty quickly

348
00:21:14,940 --> 00:21:17,420
if you're in the right kind of troop

349
00:21:17,420 --> 00:21:18,600
or the wrong kind of troop.

350
00:21:19,300 --> 00:21:22,940
And, boy, I'm being very, very general

351
00:21:22,940 --> 00:21:23,840
in my descriptions.

352
00:21:24,840 --> 00:21:26,900
But what it really comes down to

353
00:21:26,900 --> 00:21:28,620
is supporting your son.

354
00:21:29,300 --> 00:21:32,280
Is his experience meeting his expectations?

355
00:21:32,740 --> 00:21:34,700
Is he doing the things that he wants to do?

356
00:21:34,860 --> 00:21:36,060
Is he happy?

357
00:21:36,060 --> 00:21:37,960
Is he there with his buddies?

358
00:21:38,679 --> 00:21:41,040
You might want to just leave things as they are.

359
00:21:41,520 --> 00:21:43,580
If not, hey, go troop shopping.

360
00:21:43,740 --> 00:21:44,520
Find another troop.

361
00:21:45,220 --> 00:21:47,280
So after I sent this advice,

362
00:21:47,379 --> 00:21:48,580
I did get a reply back.

363
00:21:49,179 --> 00:21:50,740
And she said that, yeah,

364
00:21:51,200 --> 00:21:52,720
you know, she admitted that number one

365
00:21:52,720 --> 00:21:53,580
really doesn't work.

366
00:21:53,700 --> 00:21:56,020
And she's tried that with her older son's troop.

367
00:21:56,800 --> 00:21:59,840
And number two is what he wants.

368
00:22:00,399 --> 00:22:02,659
And it bothers me, she writes,

369
00:22:02,660 --> 00:22:04,320
the most, I guess,

370
00:22:04,380 --> 00:22:06,020
because I think it's a pretty simple formula

371
00:22:06,020 --> 00:22:06,920
to follow the program

372
00:22:06,920 --> 00:22:08,920
and people have to add their ego to it

373
00:22:08,920 --> 00:22:10,320
and I think it needs to be changed.

374
00:22:10,760 --> 00:22:13,360
Well, yeah, that's the way it is a lot of places.

375
00:22:14,040 --> 00:22:16,880
So she has decided that she is going to let things

376
00:22:16,880 --> 00:22:18,280
be as they are

377
00:22:18,280 --> 00:22:21,060
and let her son experience scouting.

378
00:22:21,440 --> 00:22:23,080
And she's going to do her best

379
00:22:23,080 --> 00:22:26,500
to work on that along with him.

380
00:22:26,500 --> 00:22:30,440
And I hope it all worked out successfully.

381
00:22:30,440 --> 00:22:31,440
Thank you.

